1585:- The count is for SETTLED phases, not for raw successive duty frames (r148 F13 is REFUTED; r151 line 24). Successive duty views need not be nested (R1 frozen views, or the trees `Σ.T` of different ALFS nodes). So the theorem is stated over the two EVIDENCE BITS of a view, `E_J` (a carrier of the top pair at `m−1`) and `E_C` (a height-`m` block that does not extend that J), with the hypothesis that each bit persists once true. Nested views are a restricted case (`twoChanges_nested`, a partial helper).
1590:- `phaseOf`, `EJ`, `EC`, `nFrame`, `effFrame_of_bits`, `twoChanges`, `twoChanges_count`, `twoChanges_nested`, `Fmove_atFrontier`: the CONTROLS `fjControls F V` of a block set V. In ALFS, V is a node's one admitted tree `Σ.T` (Lean `st.TF`), and `storeControls_eq_fjControls` (Task 7) makes these the node's live controls. Across nodes the trees need not be nested, which is why `twoChanges` is stated over the evidence bits. At one node `Σ.T` only grows (DC: the tree is cumulative; an F advance deletes no block, and `act(Σ)` is only a view), so `twoChanges_nested` covers one node while F is fixed.
1591:- `Fmove_filtered`: `filteredFrom` with ANY block set (the frozen HEAD tree or the full tree), under fixed controls in which only F moves (ldp §9.3 (1), claim C1, lines 630–640; in ALFS an F acceptance does not change `Σ.hmax`, `Σ.J` or the contest bit, ldp §4.3 L3 and Task 7). This is the pinned form of item 3 (i).
