2119:## Out of scope (later work)
2125:- The ALFS HEAD block set and its anchor. The HEAD filters DC's frozen voter tree with the full-store controls; the walk start `live_root` is AP data. The filtered frozen tree is NOT always nonempty: a late contest can set `lo = H` while every frozen block is below `H`; then the domain is empty and the HEAD returns its anchor (ldp L6, lines 354–356). This module proves the pure part: `filteredFrom` lemmas for any block set (Tasks 7, 13), including `filteredFrom_Z_mem` (D ≠ ∅ and `F ⪯ Z` give Z ∈ D in an ancestor-closed set), and nonemptiness on the full store tree `Σ.T` only (`storeFrame_feasible`). The filtered base (r161): the active view `act(Σ)` (Lean `activeView`) and every AP rule that reads it (resolution, confirmation, `reconcile_with_finality` on leases, saved results and S) are AP data. The optional deletion of blocks outside the active view (alfs4 lines 368–369) is a paper claim at `a ≤ f`; this module does not model it.
2126:- `ap.headReachesLo.v5` (registry `648f255`; v2, v3 and v4 are SUPERSEDED): the ALFS service fact, with the filtered base and DC's receipt premise with receiver exclusion. For a HEAD duty with frozen voter tree V, store controls (Z, lo), filtered domain D_V and anchor A = `live_root`: (1) if A ∈ D_V, or A has an eligible child in D_V, the head is in D_V with state height ≥ lo; (2) otherwise the head is A, which can lie outside the walked tree; (3) if A = Z and D_V ≠ ∅, then Z ∈ D_V. Clauses 1–3 are those of v2, v3 and v4, with the same numbers. Clauses 4–6 are comp/AP work and not a dependency of this plan. It is an AP fact, not a pin of this module.
2133:## Later work (SA instance)
2135:- Under ALFS, the SA obligation is `ap.headReachesLo.v5` clauses 1–3 (registry SA discharge, with the `alfs4` lines): clause 1 with `filteredFrom_reachesLo` and `filteredFrom_viable_child` on the frozen voter tree (ancestor-closed); clause 2 is `ghost`'s anchor rule; clause 3 with `filteredFrom_Z_mem` (`F ⪯ Z` from `StoreInv.FJ`). Clauses 4–6 are comp/AP work; this plan does not depend on them. In the view form, SA discharges `ap.headReachesLo.v1`, with `fj.frameFeasible.v1` parts (1)–(4) (Task 7). SA's rule: a child of a block with state height `< lo` is eligible without a majority. In a contest (`lo = H`) a child of a height-`(H−1)` block is eligible; in the uncontested or gap view (`lo = H−1`) it is not. The test that the async review (B1) asked for belongs here, because eligibility is SA's rule.
