  1149	  - `storeInv_on_block`:
  1150	    - Split on the branch of `on_block`. Refused (`B ∈ TF`, or `B.parent ∉ TF`, or `F ⋠ B`): the store does not change, so the invariant is the old one, and no `ViewRootInj` is used. Accepted: `B ∉ TF`, `B.parent ∈ TF` and `F ⪯ B`; `hinj` gives `ViewRootInj (insert B st.TF)` for `pair`.
  1151	    - `closed`: `B.parent ∈ TF` (the parent check), and the tree only grows.
  1152	    - `gen`: the tree only grows.
  1153	    - `Fmem`: F moves only to `σ.F ∈ acceptViable ⊆ TF`.
  1154	    - `hmax`: `frontier (insert B TF) = max (frontier TF) (h B)`, and `update_finality` sets `h_max := max h_max (h B)`. No block leaves the tree, so `h_max` stays the frontier (DC line 864). A refused block changes nothing (G04).
  1155	    - `pair`: a new pair enters only if `F ⪯ σ.J` and it is lex-greater; otherwise the old pair stays the lex-max over the larger tree. When F advances to `σ.F ⪯ J`, the cached pair still has `F ⪯ J`. Every other pair with `new F ⪯ J'` also had `old F ⪯ J'`, because `old F ⪯ new F`. So the lex-max does not change. A stored block that conflicts with the new F has no pair with `new F ⪯ J'`, so it cannot be selected. `hinj` makes the selected pair unique.
  1156	    - `Fcar`: at an acceptance, `B ∈ TF` (it was just accepted) and `(derive B).F = σ.F`. Otherwise F does not change and `TF` grows. `derive` is a function of the block, so the carrier keeps its F.
