   352	\paragraph{Trees.}  $\Sigma.\T$ is DC's admitted tree, with the same
   353	name and the same rules as in~\DC{7}.  It is parent-closed and
   354	cumulative: a new block enters it only if it extends~$F$, and no block
   355	leaves it~\cite{DC}.  A node never computes the state of, or unpacks, a
   356	block that does not extend its~$F$.  The \emph{active view} is
   357	\[
   358	 \act(\Sigma)=\{B\in\Sigma.\T: B\preceq\Sigma.F\ \text{or}\ \Sigma.F\preceq B\}.
   359	\]
   360	The SA base reads only the active view: the gate, release, resolution,
   361	saved-result tests, leases, and the confirmation walk~\cite[\S2]{FB}.
   362	Thus a node ignores every block that conflicts with its finality.  The
   363	FG functions read $\Sigma.\T$ as in~\DC{7}; their filters already
   364	require $\Sigma.F\preceq B$.  The caches $\Sigma.\hmax$ and the contest
   365	test read the cumulative $\Sigma.\T$, as the caches of~\DC{5} do.  A
   366	block of $\Sigma.\T$ outside the active view with height above
   367	$\Sigma.h_F$ needs a slashable conflict (\textsf{fg.finalLock}).  A
   368	node can delete blocks outside the active view; with $a\leq f$ this
   369	changes no output.  The confirmation walk starts at genesis.  The FJ
   370	viability and band filter is a further filter for HEAD, proposal, and
   371	FG duties; it does not restrict the SA confirmation walk.
   372	
   373	\paragraph{Block states and FG caches.}  $\Sigma.\sigma[B]$ is the
   374	immutable post-state of an admitted block~$B$, the chain state
   375	of~\DC{4}:
   443	an ancestor has a deadline at least as late, and a vote that conflicts
   444	with an ancestor also conflicts with the descendant~\LDP{1}.
   445	$\Sigma.\fastWrite[r]$ is new: the set of blocks to which the gate
   446	at~$d_r$ wrote or renewed a lease by the fast test~\FAST{3.1}.  The
   447	gate creates it once, as the empty set when the result is empty or
   448	vetoed.  Reconciliation removes incompatible targets from every such set.  A slow renewal alone does not put a block in it.  A renewal
   449	counts also when the maximum leaves the stored deadline unchanged.
   450	
   451	\paragraph{Cached and derived.}  Besides the tree, the stamps, and
   452	the pools, the store caches these fields: the block states
   453	$\Sigma.\sigma$; the SA fields $\Sigma.\genuine$, $\Sigma.\lease$,
   454	$\Sigma.\fastWrite$, and $\Sigma.\latestConfirmed$; and the FG caches
