   853	
   854	The store adds a block state map $\Sigma.\sigma[\cdot]$ and finality state
   855	$(\Sigma.F,\Sigma.J,\Sigma.h_j,\Sigma.\hmax)$.
   856	Figure~\ref{alg:fg-store} extends the block handler: it admits only
   857	descendants of the finalized block, computes and stores
   858	the post-state, then folds it into the finality caches with
   859	$\Call{update\_finality}{\Sigma,\sigma}$.  The pair
   860	$(\Sigma.J,\Sigma.h_j)$ tracks the lex-greatest justification event
   861	compatible with the finalized block.  $\Sigma.F$ advances
   862	only to a viable proper descendant of itself below~$\Sigma.J$, so
   863	$\Sigma.F\preceq\Sigma.J$ always holds and finalization never reverts.
   864	$\Sigma.\hmax$ only grows, and every block that raises it descends the
   865	finalized block at that moment.  When $\Sigma.F$ advances, an admitted
   866	block can stop descending it and its branch freezes: its children now
   867	fail admission.  The viability guard on the advance then keeps
   868	$\Sigma.\hmax$ at most one above the largest state height among the
   869	finalized block's descendants, so $\Sigma.F$ itself is always viable.
