  2093	  - A `CHANGED` line means that a source changed after registration. Compare the pinned text of each entry that cites it. The registry gives a new id only when the statement or its hypotheses change; otherwise the async session updates the hash.
  2094	  - `KEY NOT IN §0.1`, `PATH NOT IN §0.1 ROW` or `HASH NOT IN §0.1 ROW` means that a `Src` does not match its registered source: fix the `Src`, or ask the async session.
  2095	  - `NO REGISTRY ENTRY` means that an id in `Pins.lean` has no entry: fix the id, or ask the async session.
  2096	  - `SUPERSEDED` means that a pinned id has a newer id in the registry: re-pin to the new id (read its entry and its "Change against" note), or ask the async session. `ID NOT EXACTLY ONCE IN INDEX` means that the Index table has no row, or more than one row, for the id: ask the async session.
