   822	  `lexMax E cfg F Vw` returns the lex-greatest `(h_j, J)` over `W ∈ Vw` with `F ⪯ (derive W).J`, or `(0, genesis)` if there is none:
   823	  - Compute the greatest key with `Finset.sup` over `Lex (ℕ × ℕ)`.
   824	  - Take the pair with that key through `pickPair`, a port of DC's `pickUnique?` (`DC/DecoupledConsensusModel/Objects/Blocks.lean:295–301`), on the Finset of candidate PAIRS (the image of the view, so that two carriers of one pair count once), with `(0, genesis)` as the default.
   825	  - `pickPair` has DC's tie behavior: it returns the unique candidate with the greatest key, and `none` when two DISTINCT candidates have that key (a root collision). Then `lexMax` falls back to `(0, genesis)`. Do not choose one of them: there is no computable order on `FGBlock` that the spec names.
   826	  - Under `ViewRootInj Vw`, two candidates with one key are one pair (same `h_j`, same root, so the same J), so `pickPair` returns it. Every lemma that reads the selected pair (`lexMax_of_candidate`, `lexMax_mono`, `storeControls_eq_fjControls`, `fjFrame_D_nonempty`, the Task 12 and 13 lemmas) has `ViewRootInj` as a hypothesis.
   827	  - Keep `lexMax` computable, so that the `decide` examples reduce.
   828	
   829	  The fallback `(0, genesis)`: if `F ≠ genesis` and no pair in the view extends F, then `J = genesis`, and `F ⪯ J` fails. In ALFS the controls come from the full store, which holds the block that finalized F (`StoreInv.Fcar`, Task 7), so the fallback is not used there. Task 7's `lexMax_of_candidate` (a helper) proves that the fallback is not used when the block set holds a block whose J extends F and `ViewRootInj` holds. Keep the fallback; do not change it to `(h_F, F)`, because the spec does not say so.
   830	
   831	
   832	  Write `fjFrame` through the two parts, and keep its fields:
   833	
   834	```lean
   835	/-- [pin fj.frame.v1] The controls of one block set (r148 §2 FJ_FRAME, R1 view
   836	form): H, the lex pair with `F ⪯ J`, and the contest at `H = j+1` when a
   837	height-H block does not extend J. -/
   838	def fjControls (F : FGBlock V) (Vw : View V) : Controls V :=
   839	  let H := frontier E cfg Vw
   840	  let p := lexMax E cfg F Vw
   841	  ⟨F, H, p.1, p.2, decide (H = p.1 + 1) &&
   842	    decide (∃ W ∈ Vw, hOf E cfg W = H ∧ ¬ FGBlock.Preceq p.2 W)⟩
   843	
   844	/-- [pin fj.frame.v3] The filtered tree of any block set under given controls
   845	(`get_filtered_block_tree_from(Σ, blocks)` with `viable_tree_from`, alfs4 lines
   846	988–994, 1013–1020). -/
   847	def filteredFrom (c : Controls V) (blocks : Finset (FGBlock V)) : Finset (FGBlock V) :=
   848	  blocks.filter (fun B => FGBlock.preceq c.F B && FGBlock.preceq c.Z B &&
   849	    decide (∃ W ∈ blocks, FGBlock.Preceq B W ∧ c.lo ≤ hOf E cfg W))
   850	
   851	/-- [pin fj.frame.v1] The special case: controls and filtered tree from one
   852	block set. -/
   853	def fjFrame (F : FGBlock V) (Vw : View V) : Frame V :=
   854	  let c := fjControls E cfg F Vw
   855	  ⟨c.F, c.H, c.j, c.J, c.Z, c.lo, filteredFrom E cfg c Vw, c.contest⟩
   856	```
