lean/available-chain/docs/audit/fg-plan-audit-report.md:75:The spec separates the raw tree from the FG-admitted tree. It inserts a block into the latter and calls `update_finality` only if the current `F ⪯ B`. The plan calls its tree “processed” and inserts every block passed to `on_block`; its stated precondition concerns only the parent. An off-F branch can therefore raise `h_max`, enter duty views, and change the frame. Ordinary block validity does not supply the missing FG guard. Either enforce the guard or expose an explicitly named admission operation whose contract requires it. [Spec:338](/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/spec/fgsa-protocol.tex:338), [Spec:694](/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/spec/fgsa-protocol.tex:694), [Plan:655](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/plans/2026-09-28-fg-module.md:655).
lean/available-chain/docs/audit/fg-plan-audit-report.md:77:**G05 — The F-basis lemma assumes the property that the store must establish.**  
lean/available-chain/docs/audit/fg-plan-audit-report.md:82:**G06 — `provenance_finality` proves a different fact.**  
lean/available-chain/docs/audit/fg-plan-audit-report.md:87:**G07 — Growing views do not express the registered settled-phase result.**  
lean/available-chain/docs/audit/fg-plan-audit-report.md:92:**G08 — `.full` has no consistent meaning in the pin table.**  
lean/available-chain/docs/audit/fg-plan-audit-report.md:95:- `fjFrame_lo` proves one projection equation, but its pin says `.full`.
lean/available-chain/docs/audit/fg-plan-audit-report.md:96:- `accountable` and F monotonicity omit the pinned `finalized ⪯ available` accessor result. That result belongs outside this frame-only module; record the omission.
lean/available-chain/docs/audit/fg-plan-audit-report.md:97:- `uniqueJust` exports general slashable evidence. It does not export the pinned E2-specific evidence or whole-run uniqueness. The review accepts the DC certificate form, but “full Lean part” must remain distinct from full registry coverage.
lean/available-chain/docs/audit/fg-plan-audit-report.md:103:**G09 — The checker can report success without checking pins.**  
lean/available-chain/docs/audit/fg-plan-audit-report.md:104:I ran the proposed shell body in memory with the pin input set to an empty file and then a nonexistent path. Both runs returned status 0. Failures inside the process substitution do not update `status`, and an empty extraction produces no checks. Hash-half searches also do not bind a hash to its registered source path.
lean/available-chain/docs/audit/fg-plan-audit-report.md:106:All eight proposed `Src` hashes currently match. The spec and DC paper hashes also match the registry. However, neither is in the proposed `Src` list, although the spec controls executable behavior and `frameCompat` cites both. Add explicit executable-source pins, reject missing or empty input, and check exact source associations. A changed file hash requires comparison; it does not always require a new registry id. The registry requires a new id when the statement or hypotheses change. [Plan:1203](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/plans/2026-09-28-fg-module.md:1203), [Registry policy:8](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/FG-COMPOSITION.md:8).
